      "id": "lb9zq7u",
      "type": "heading",
      "level": 2,
      "content": "1. Meaning of Economic Planning"
    },
    {
      "type": "keyFacts",
      "title": "Key Takeaways",
      "items": [
        "Economic planning in India was structured around long-term development objectives such as growth, modernization, self-reliance, and equity.",
        "The Planning Commission was responsible for formulating Five-Year Plans to allocate resources effectively across sectors.",
        "NITI Aayog replaced the Planning Commission to serve as a modern policy think tank promoting cooperative federalism.",
        "The shift to NITI Aayog introduced a bottom-up approach to policy framing, giving states a stronger voice in national planning."
      ],
      "id": "ddz6i09"
    },
